    "observations": {
      "base-fixed-spread": "Clear thin branching structure, two main side canopies with many small terminal forks.",
      "narrowing-spread": "Same branching pattern but later twigs align more tightly; generation-dependent angular control is visible without changing topology.",
      "depth-6": "Fewer total segments but later branch layout is also rearranged, including the upper silhouette. This is shared DFS random-stream drift, not a clean prune of the baseline.",
      "wider-spread-0.9": "Much wider, more horizontal canopy; geometry remains inside the canvas in this case.",
      "recolour-base": "Early branches remain muted while tips become coral; generation attributes make independent colour styling useful.",
      "tapered-terminal-base": "Thicker trunk and tapering limbs read clearly; coral terminal dots include early-death tips while preserving the exact baseline geometry.",
      "binary-slots": "Narrow upright spray; changing slot count/rule produces a substantially different idiom with the same retained expansion/drawing structure.",
      "circle-transfer": "Seven independent structures at placement-derived roots, including one bare stem; the same branch kernel transfers successfully. Root separation does not imply separated canopies."
    }
